# POC-VMS-41 post-hoc diagnostic audit checklist

- Confirm this module was created after the live VMS-41 bundle and is excluded from the preexecution freeze.
- Confirm the source live bundle is opened read-only and independently replayed before sealing or verifying the diagnostic bundle.
- Confirm the disclosed blindness state is exactly `BREACHED_BEFORE_MANUAL_AUDIT`, the purpose is exactly `FAILURE_LOCALIZATION_ONLY`, and `confirmation_eligible` can never become true.
- Confirm the only component verdict allowed by the review, summary, receipt and verifier is `NOT_QUALIFIED`.
- Confirm all four frozen case IDs and attempt IDs occur exactly once and bind candidate, export, invocation and evaluation hashes.
- Confirm the diagnostic audit is append-once, uses a private partial directory, fsyncs, seals with an artifact tree and COMMITTED marker, and rejects symlinks, unknown files and tampering.
- Confirm an existing identical final audit is only verified and never overwritten; a partial root is preserved for manual recovery.
- Confirm no model, Solver, DB, Redis, Seven, network or subagent call occurs.
- Confirm the old frozen tool verdict remains intact and post-hoc tool classification is stored separately.
- Confirm the audit cannot authorize retrying any VMS-41 attempt.
